. Its diameter is nearly constant, with a slight flare at the base and a mild taper toward the crown.", "The render trunk has no foliage, epiphytes or branches. The only features are sparse, small leaf-base knobs.", "Each render crown has about 20–30 pinnate fronds radiating from the apex. Upper fronds point upward and outward, and the lower ones droop past the point where the trunk meets the crown.", "In render-2 the frond tips droop more than in the whole-tree views, but frond length relative to the trunk stays short compared with reference-0.", "Render-3 (P-BASE) has a visibility value of 'hidden' in its metadata, but the image clearly shows a close view of the trunk surface with about 5 isolated stubs.", "There is no dead-frond skirt beneath the crown (a secondary trait) and no crownshaft, which matches crown-shaft-absent.", "The render foliage is deep green, within the variation seen in reference-0. The straight, vertical trunk falls within the observed lean range (reference-1 and reference-2 are straight).", "The finish is clean, shaded geometry, broadly comparable to the anchor-0 floor. The anchor is used only for finish quality, not morphology."], "findings": [{"observation": "The crown reads as a pinnate rosette, and its lowest fronds droop below the crown base. However, the fronds are short, mostly straight and stiffly spiky, without the long arching recurve seen in the references.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and leaflet size may still be below the reference proportions; the owner names these as the first dials."}, {"observation": "In the close crown view, leaflets are broad, lanceolate and soft-looking in a flat plane rather than narrow, stiff and V-sectioned. In the whole-tree views, the margins do look bristly.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": true